  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe program sim's gouge verdict judged each column by height alone, at its centre. A height verdict's normal-distance tolerance is `tol * cos(slope)`, which is zero at a vertical wall. So a column whose centre sits a few microns inside a wall, reached by a tool that finishes that wall within tolerance, was charged the wall's whole height, and the post gate refused a correct program.\n\n- New `crates/sim/src/stock_sim/wall_slack.rs`: a gouge candidate (a column more than `tol` below the part's top at its centre) is re-judged against the lowest part top within `tol` of its centre. That is the centre plus an eight-direction ring at radius `tol`, and air counts as lowest. If the column is within `tol` of that lowest top, it is clean. Otherwise it is a gouge, charged at the centre's own depth as before.\n- Both engines use it: the column engine (`deviate`) and the field arm (`deviate_field`), keeping the stage-C parity law.\n- Rest is unchanged: it is still judged against the centre's own top.\n- The extra cost is paid only when gouge candidates exist. A clean program costs nothing extra.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/299-wall-column-gouge.md`. It covers why the slack is `tol` and not the issue's `gate_tol(DEV_TOL, cell)`, and the other options that were dropped.\n\n## Readings (current main 5fd2b93)\n\n- The issue's exact 2D Contour repro (model stock, 10 mm deep) **no longer reproduces on main**: the gate is clean before and after this change. It is kept as a regression test.\n- 3D Finish, `BN-0600`, kind defaults, model stock (the issue's MCP job): before, `gouge: ... 1 cell(s), worst 10.21 mm at (16.69, -24.91, z 9.79)`. Probing that column, its centre is 1-3 um inside the D's wall, with air beyond. After: no gouge. The post is still blocked, by the generator's own `ShankHit` warnings, which is a separate matter.\n- 3D Finish in the issue's 70 x 70 x 27 box at z -7: before, 37 cells, worst 22.01 mm at (-26.56, 13.94). After: 0 gouge cells.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `crates/sim/tests/wall_slack.rs` (new, 5 tests):\n  - `a_column_a_few_microns_inside_a_finished_wall_is_not_a_gouge`: both engines, with a floor beside the wall and with air beside it. This test fails on main.\n  - `the_old_law_charged_that_column_the_whole_wall`\n  - `a_real_gouge_into_a_wall_still_convicts_at_its_full_depth`: covers 50 um, 12 um and 1 mm intrusions, in both engines, and checks the full 15 mm depth and location.\n  - `a_floor_gouge_away_from_walls_is_unchanged`\n  - `rest_beside_a_wall_keeps_the_centres_own_top`\n- `crates/app/tests/wall_column_gouge.rs` (new, 3 tests):\n  - `a_3d_finish_on_the_users_part_reads_no_gouge_at_its_wall`: fails on main.\n  - `a_3d_finish_in_the_users_box_stock_reads_no_gouge_at_its_wall`: fails on main.\n  - `the_issues_contour_on_model_stock_reads_no_gouge`\n- Gate results:\n  - `cargo test -p camcraft-sim`: all green.\n  - `cargo test -p camcraft-app` (all 169 binaries, debug): all green.\n  - `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app --all-targets -D warnings`: clean.\n- Release `--ignored` lanes:\n  - sim `hidden_rest_banded`, app `operations` and `rotary_field_parity`: green.\n  - app `stock_engine_agreement` has 2 tests (`both_engines_judge_every_golden_program_alike`, `the_feed_sampler_reads_every_golden_program_alike`) that **fail identically on upstream/main** (6467 FINDING lines, for example `contour_disc_hole.cl` column (46.25, -4.25) and `finish3d_scallop_plateau.cl+bull` engagement). This is pre-existing and not caused by this PR. Diffing the findings between main and this branch shows 5 lines changed: field-arm micro-readings on `finish3d_project_dome.cl` (field dev -0.011 to -0.016 on the slope) now read clean instead of gouge. That is the expected slope allowance (at most `tol * tan(slope)`). No column-engine verdict changed, and no golden changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- GUI Deviate view, by eye.\n- A real cut.\n- `kernel::measure` / `measure_field` (the per-op reports, not the post gate) keep the centre-only law.\n- #303 (chamfer/deburr false gouge) is **not** fixed by this. Its bevel is a sloped cut 0.74-3.8 mm deep, far past a 10 um slack, and needs the op-owns-its-break law the issue describes.\n\nChangelog: The post gate no longer refuses a correct program for a gouge at a wall: a sim column within the 0.01 mm tolerance of a vertical wall is judged against the floor beside it, while a cut past that still refuses (#299)\n\nFixes #299\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
